<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">José Tomás Boves</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1782">1782</a>–<a href="/years/1814">1814</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">José Tomás Boves was a Spanish-born royalist commander in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venezuelan-war-of-independence">Venezuelan War of Independence</a>. Leading an army of llaneros, the horsemen of the plains, he turned the war into a brutal social conflict against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/criollo-people">Creole</a> elite and defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> at La Puerta in June 1814, destroying the Second Republic of Venezuela. He was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-urica">Battle of Urica</a> in December 1814.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jose-tomas-boves.jpg" alt="José Tomás Boves" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jos%C3%A9_Tom%C3%A1s_Boves_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
